keyboard-workshop - licensing
=============================

Copyright (c) 2026 baal (github.com/baalsmn)

This repository holds open hardware designs and the tools that make them.

Hardware designs - CERN-OHL-S-2.0
---------------------------------
Everything that describes the physical keyboards is licensed under the
CERN Open Hardware Licence Version 2 - Strongly Reciprocal (CERN-OHL-S-2.0),
full text in LICENSES/CERN-OHL-S-2.0.txt. This covers:

  - the Ergogen designs (ergogen/*.yaml) and keyboard layouts (*/kle/),
  - the Ergogen footprints in footprints/ (see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md for the
    ones derived from other open sources),
  - the case outputs (*/case/: STL, STEP, Fusion data), the PCBs and KiCad files
    (*/kicad/, kicad-libraries/, keyboard.kicad_dru),
  - the 3D models made for this project in kicad-libraries/3dmodels/ (recreated from public
    datasheet dimensions by tools/lib/make_models.py, and the generated keycap
    and OLED models),
  - documentation, renders, printouts and drafts.

Software - GPL-3.0-or-later
---------------------------
The scripts in tools/ (shell, Python, JavaScript, the Fusion script) are free
software: you can redistribute and/or modify them under the terms of the GNU
General Public License as published by the Free Software Foundation, either
version 3 of the License, or (at your option) any later version. They are
distributed WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY. Full text: LICENSES/GPL-3.0.txt.

Third-party material
--------------------
Some files come from, or are derived from, other projects under their own
licences (KiCad libraries: CC-BY-SA-4.0; 0xCB Helios: CERN-OHL-S-2.0;
ceoloide's ergogen-footprints: MIT). They keep those licences; see
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

Not covered / not included
--------------------------
Vendor datasheets (datasheets/*.pdf) remain the property of their
manufacturers and are not covered by these licences; datasheets/LINKS.md lists
where to get them. Vendor 3D models and logo artwork are kept out of the
repository (vendor/: gitignored). Product names and
trademarks belong to their owners.
